 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Decorator:** `needs_app_scope`, defined at `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It wraps the callback so the app is loaded and its app context is active before the callback runs.\n\nYou only need it explicitly on plain `click` commands. Commands registered with `@app.cli.command()` or `@bundle.cli.command()` get it automatically, because `AppGroup.command` (`src/tessel/cli.py:413`) wraps them. Pass `needs_app_scope=False` to opt out.\n\n**Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` in `src/tessel/cli.py:293`. Its `load_app()` method (`src/tessel/cli.py:333`) loads the app, and `needs_app_scope` calls it via `ctx.ensure_object(LaunchInfo).load_app()`.\n\n`TesselGroup` (`src/tessel/cli.py:531`) is the top-level CLI group, and it subclasses `AppGroup`.",
